-------------------------------------------------------------
All original files, formal proofs, optimization passes, translation validation
checkers, certificate schemas, IR bridges, orchestration tools, build scripts,
and modifications authored for the LLVMCert project (collectively, the
"LLVMCert Proprietary Software") are dual-licensed under EITHER:

  (a) The LLVMCert Non-Commercial Evaluation & Research License Agreement set
      forth below (permitting strictly non-commercial academic, educational,
      and internal evaluation use only); OR

  (b) A separate written LLVMCert Commercial Software License Agreement
      executed with the copyright holder, which is MANDATORY for any commercial
      use, production builds, safety-critical qualification, internal business
      operations, or hosted/SaaS compilation services.

To obtain a Commercial Software License Agreement, contact the repository
owner (@mannomannX).

2. THIRD-PARTY OPEN-SOURCE COMPONENTS IN THIS REPOSITORY
--------------------------------------------------------
Upstream third-party files included in this repository retain their respective
copyrights and open-source licenses:

  * LLVM, Clang, LLD, CMake modules, libc shared headers, libunwind headers,
    and SipHash (`llvm/`, `clang/`, `lld/`, `cmake/`, `libc/`, `libunwind/`,
    `third-party/siphash/`):
    Distributed under the Apache License v2.0 with LLVM Exceptions.
    See `LICENSE-LLVM.TXT` and `llvm/LICENSE.TXT`.

  * Vellvm Rocq formal semantics & AST utilities (`vellvm/src/rocq/Syntax/`,
    `Semantics/`, `Theory/`, `Utils/`, `vellvm/src/ml/extracted/`, and MIT
    helper modules in `vellvm/src/ml/`):
    Copyright (c) Vellvm developers, distributed under the MIT License.
    See `vellvm/LICENSE.md`.

  * Vellvm surface IR lexer and parser (`vellvm/src/ml/libvellvm/llvm_lexer.mll`,
    `vellvm/src/ml/libvellvm/llvm_parser.mly`):
    Distributed under the ISC License (preserved in each file header).

  * CompCert numeric formalizations (`vellvm/src/rocq/Numeric/*.v`):
    Copyright Institut National de Recherche en Informatique et en Automatique
    (INRIA), dual-licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License v2.1 or
    later (`LGPL-2.1-or-later`) and the INRIA Non-Commercial License Agreement.
    For commercial distributions, LLVMCert elects the `LGPL-2.1-or-later`
    option as indicated in each file header.

Nothing in the LLVMCert Non-Commercial Evaluation & Research License Agreement
restricts your rights under the applicable upstream open-source licenses solely
with respect to unmodified third-party files listed above.

